   "body": "Result (coordinator; `solver/harmony/stokes/second_zero_nodes.py`, raw `harmony-mac/stokes/second_zero_nodes.log` at e870b95; notes/HARMONY.md, fa61488).\n\nOn the seven nodes (\u03c3\u2080\u2026\u03c3\u2081\u2086 at \u03c9/\u03c9\u221e 1.06\u20131.14), Im x\u2081 changes sign in every Borel\u2013Pad\u00e9 sum [m/(16\u2212m)], m = 5\u20269, at \u03c9/\u03c9\u221e = 1.0962\u20131.1001 (x\u2081 \u2248 13.4, A \u2248 3.66). The criterion set in comms holds on the data.\n\n**Both controls fail**, so this is not established:\n- crossing planted at 1.095: found at 1.0962 and 1.1013 by four sums, 1.0698 by [5/11] (tolerance 0.005);\n- crossing planted at 1.15: [5/11] reports a false crossing at 1.1248; the other sums correctly report none.\n\nAt 17 coefficients the method resolves a crossing to about \u00b10.006 and [5/11] is unreliable. The candidate second selected solution (\u0394 \u2248 1.50) stays a candidate; the follow-up is a separate issue.",
